# Sleepless passwordless grant — template.
#
# install.sh substitutes __USER__ with your login name ($(id -un)) and installs
# the result to /etc/sudoers.d/sleepless-disablesleep, owned root:wheel, mode 0440.
#
# It grants ONE user the right to run, as root, EXACTLY these fully-specified commands and
# NOTHING else. sudoers matches command arguments literally (there are no wildcards here),
# so this grant cannot be widened by appending other flags: `sudo pmset -a sleep 0`,
# `pmset restoredefaults`, `launchctl bootout system/<anything else>`, etc. all fall through
# and demand a password. What it lets Sleepless do without a prompt:
#   - flip lid-close sleep on (1) or off (0)
#   - set Energy Mode: High Power (on) or Automatic (off)
#   - start, stop, restart, or remove its own optional background service (the LaunchDaemon
#     plist is root-owned, so these commands cannot load anything else; the two `rm` commands
#     name only the service's own files, so `brew uninstall` can remove it without a prompt)
# See SECURITY.md for the full threat model.
__USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/pmset -a disablesleep 0, /usr/bin/pmset -a disablesleep 1, /usr/bin/pmset -a powermode 2, /usr/bin/pmset -a powermode 0, /bin/launchctl enable system/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer, /bin/launchctl disable system/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer, /bin/launchctl bootstrap system /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer.plist, /bin/launchctl bootout system/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer, /bin/launchctl kickstart -k system/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer, /bin/rm -f /Library/LaunchDaemons/com.aboudjem.Sleepless.timer.plist, /bin/rm -rf /Library/Application\ Support/Sleepless
